==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
Known since 1655, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|alimonia||food, support, nourishment, sustenance}} (English {{m|en|aliment}}, as in {{m|en|alimentary}}), itself from {{m|la|alere||to nourish}} + {{m|la|-monia||action, state, condition}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈælɪməni/|lang=en}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˈælɪmoʊni/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-alimony.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|alimonies}}

# {{lb|en|legal}} A [[court]]-[[mandate]]d [[allowance]] made to a [[former]] [[spouse]] by a [[divorce]]d or [[legally]] [[separated]] person.
# The [[means]] to [[support]] [[life]].

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|allowance to a former spouse}} [[maintenance]]

